WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.229
- Welcome back y'all we've
got Tiffany Haddish dialed in,

00:00:03.229 --> 00:00:04.112
give it up for her.

00:00:04.112 --> 00:00:05.690
(audience applauding)

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.900
So we're celebrating
Rad Mamas all week long

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.570
and Tiffany's new kid's book
is perfect for all you mamas.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.070
It's called "Layla the Last Black Unicorn".

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:14.903
I love it.

00:00:14.903 --> 00:00:17.610
The colorful cause my kids love color.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.850
It's a great story that comes

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.610
with some very cool illustrations.

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.450
It reminded us of a segment we like to do

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:24.977
at the show for guests
who have stories so epic

00:00:24.977 --> 00:00:27.370
there's just not enough
time to tell them properly.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:28.720
So just so happens.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.300
Tiffany is one of those guests
with one of those stories.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.537
So we now bring you another
installment of Epic Story Time

00:00:35.537 --> 00:00:37.120
(upbeat music)

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.574
- ♪Epic story time. ♪

00:00:39.574 --> 00:00:40.830
(audience applauding)

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.720
- All right. So with this
segment I ask one question

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.920
and Tiffany will tell
us an epic story backed

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.590
by a bunch of illustrations.

00:00:47.590 --> 00:00:50.040
As always I'll have some
follow up questions at the end

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:52.150
but here's my one question
to get us started.

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:52.983
All right.

00:00:52.983 --> 00:00:56.140
Hey Tiffany, it's Rad
Mama week at the show.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:58.270
Have you ever thought about motherhood?

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:01.260
- Well, I definitely have thought about it

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.990
which leads me to a really amazing story.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:05.259
Let me tell you.

00:01:05.259 --> 00:01:06.092
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:06.092 --> 00:01:09.630
This story is how I ended up with a baby

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.340
in a bed with me one morning okay.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.460
It all started when I was on a date

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:15.840
we had a very good time.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.320
We were talking and laughing
and drinking wine all evening.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.740
Like I said, it was a very good time.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:24.325
So we was feeling ourselves, right.

00:01:24.325 --> 00:01:25.158
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:25.158 --> 00:01:28.730
And at what point during the
day the guy got all serious

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:32.327
and he leaned in and asked me,

00:01:32.327 --> 00:01:35.770
"are you interested in
having kids in the future?"

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:39.460
And at that moment I was
thinking, thank Lord,

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:41.699
I remember to take my birth control, okay.

00:01:41.699 --> 00:01:43.956
(audience laughing)

00:01:43.956 --> 00:01:46.789
But, I said to him very casually,

00:01:48.147 --> 00:01:51.580
"whatever God has planned
for me is what it is,

00:01:51.580 --> 00:01:53.560
maybe in the next two and three years

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.460
maybe five years from now.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:59.325
Otherwise I'm not that
interested in this exact moment."

00:01:59.325 --> 00:02:00.289
(audience laughing)

00:02:00.289 --> 00:02:04.490
So after the date, the guy drops me off

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:07.740
and kisses me at the front door

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:10.750
and it's a very romantic,
lovely little kiss.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:14.410
And I went inside and at that moment

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:16.250
I was supposed to call my sister

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:18.260
but it was around midnight

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.690
and I was exhausted and
I had been drinking.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:22.931
So I just went ahead
and went to bed, okay.

00:02:22.931 --> 00:02:23.764
(audience laughing)

00:02:23.764 --> 00:02:26.170
I went right to sleep, fell asleep.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:29.410
When I woke up the next
morning, I felt great.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:31.440
I was feeling really good.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.100
And then what was, something's crying?

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:41.240
I look over and there's a
baby on the bed lying right

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:44.827
next to me. What the hell!
Who put this baby on my bed?

00:02:44.827 --> 00:02:47.960
I start freaking out, like,
when did I have a baby?

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.812
Oh my gosh am I two to
five years in the future?

00:02:50.812 --> 00:02:51.722
(audience laughing)

00:02:51.722 --> 00:02:52.920
Then I have a baby and I
don't remember having a baby.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:56.400
I don't feel no baby pains

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.370
My stomach ain't small.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.180
Where did the baby come from?

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:00.090
Am I still dreaming?

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:01.340
Maybe I'm dreaming about this baby

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:04.010
cause the baby looked just like me.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.270
Is this my baby?

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:08.710
I called my sister.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:09.620
I called my sister.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.060
I said, "girl, there's a baby in my bed.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.490
I don't know how this baby got in my bed.

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:18.590
I don't know where this baby
came from it look just like me.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:19.780
What year is this?"

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.904
She said, "girl, it's 2016."

00:03:21.904 --> 00:03:25.680
I said, "oh, okay but okay,
well, 2016 when I went to sleep

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.730
with, where I got a baby"

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:28.980
she said, "what'd the baby look like?"

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.220
I started describing the baby.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.000
She said, "girl, that's Jasmine, baby."

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.564
That's my other sister.

00:03:34.564 --> 00:03:35.522
(audience laughing)

00:03:35.522 --> 00:03:36.467
So I called my sister Jasmine,

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:39.260
"Jasmine how'd your baby get in my bed?"

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:40.970
And she said, "you and the baby okay".

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.250
I said, "yeah, we fine but how
did the baby get in my bed?"

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:47.093
She said, "I came over about
one o'clock you said, yeah,

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.630
the baby can stay here.
I have to be at work."

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.560
I said, "oh, okay oh,
you gotta be at work.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:53.121
But I gotta a job too.

00:03:53.121 --> 00:03:56.310
You know, I have to work too."

00:03:56.310 --> 00:04:00.130
So I was working on the
Carmichael show at that time

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:03.173
and I had to take this
baby to work with me.

00:04:03.173 --> 00:04:04.840
I took the baby to work with me.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.320
I had her sitting right
next to me during the

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:10.160
table read and during rehearsals.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.300
And you know we did our table read

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.440
and everybody was looking like

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.390
why does Tiffany have this baby here?

00:04:16.390 --> 00:04:17.320
But I didn't say nothing.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.140
I just kept going through with my scene

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:21.362
and everything finished the table read.

00:04:21.362 --> 00:04:23.597
And then I stood up and I said

00:04:24.437 --> 00:04:27.200
"I have an announcement to make everyone,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.992
this is not my baby."

00:04:28.992 --> 00:04:31.291
(audience laughing)

00:04:31.291 --> 00:04:32.124
- Which then

00:04:32.124 --> 00:04:33.571
- This is my niece.
I'm babysitting.

00:04:33.571 --> 00:04:35.400
(audience laughing)

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.340
And I was bringing her to work every week

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.040
with me till my sister lost her job.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:39.934
The end.

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:40.767
(audience laughing)

00:04:40.767 --> 00:04:42.098
- Until my sister job.

00:04:42.098 --> 00:04:44.320
(audience applauding)

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.183
Oh my God.

00:04:47.771 --> 00:04:49.630
Please tell me that you (beep)

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.347
you had a pause when you said,

00:04:51.347 --> 00:04:53.040
"hey guys, this isn't my baby."

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.280
Like people were like,
"whose baby do you have?"

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.360
Like, please tell me you left a pause

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.413
before you said, "it's my niece."

00:04:59.413 --> 00:05:00.802
(both laughing)

00:05:00.802 --> 00:05:01.853
- I did pause.

00:05:01.853 --> 00:05:04.773
It was so funny because like,
everybody was like, what?

00:05:04.773 --> 00:05:06.797
Like they were whispering to each other.

00:05:06.797 --> 00:05:08.650
And I wasn't saying anything about it.

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:11.480
I wasn't talking, like I
was acting it's normal to

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:13.400
bring a baby to work, you know,

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:15.341
on the movie set.

00:05:15.341 --> 00:05:17.028
- I love that you didn't say anything.

00:05:17.028 --> 00:05:18.560
- And I gave her her bottle.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:20.130
She was chill. My niece is cool.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.020
She's just like me.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.580
She's all about entertainment.

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:25.410
You know, she was laughing
at all my jokes in the scene.

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:26.243
I was loving her.

00:05:26.243 --> 00:05:27.920
I was like, yeah, I need
her to be here all the time.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:30.140
She was only like five months too.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.480
She was a little baby.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:32.313
She should not have been there.

00:05:32.313 --> 00:05:34.070
- Oh my God.

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:36.393
Thank you for your epic story, Tiffany.

00:05:36.393 --> 00:05:37.250
(audience applauding)

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.620
That was awesome.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:42.986
And a big, thanks to Marcel
Asevedo in our department

00:05:42.986 --> 00:05:45.340
in our art department, he is amazing.

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:46.750
He did all those illustrations.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:47.723
He's so talented.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:49.710
And there's so funny.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:53.440
Tiffany's kids' book is
"Layla, the Last Black Unicorn".

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:56.430
Y'all gotta go pick it up and
her movie it's so funny y'all,

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:58.795
it's so good, "The Unbearable
Weight of Massive Talent".

00:05:58.795 --> 00:06:00.500
They're both out right now.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.780
So go check 'em out.

